WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.867
Self-attention.

2
00:00:02.167 --> 00:00:06.800
The mechanism that replaced recurrence, and powers every modern language model.

3
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.363
Self-attention turns attention inward.

4
00:00:10.363 --> 00:00:12.167
The sequence looks at itself.

5
00:00:12.467 --> 00:00:20.200
Every token computes weights over every other token, itself included, and rebuilds its representation as a weighted blend.

6
00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:22.600
Take this sentence.

7
00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:24.572
The word it is ambiguous.

8
00:00:24.572 --> 00:00:30.390
Its attention weights fall mostly on tank, so its new vector is mostly built from tank.

9
00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:33.600
Every other token does the same, simultaneously.

10
00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:35.933
Why did this win?

11
00:00:35.933 --> 00:00:37.467
Compare it with an RNN.

12
00:00:37.767 --> 00:00:42.633
An RNN passes information along step by step, and it degrades on the way.

13
00:00:42.933 --> 00:00:46.300
Self-attention connects every pair of tokens directly.

14
00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:51.133
And it is just matrix multiplication, exactly what GPUs love.

15
00:00:51.433 --> 00:00:54.767
The catch is that cost grows as n squared with sequence length.

16
00:00:55.967 --> 00:00:57.600
Here's the whole thing in NumPy.

17
00:00:57.900 --> 00:01:00.733
Six tokens, each a sixty four number embedding.

18
00:01:01.033 --> 00:01:06.133
Multiplying X by its own transpose scores every token against every token.

19
00:01:06.433 --> 00:01:11.133
Softmax turns scores into weights, and one more multiply blends the tokens.

20
00:01:11.433 --> 00:01:13.367
Same shape in, same shape out.

21
00:01:14.567 --> 00:01:16.600
Now the price of all-to-all attention.

22
00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:23.033
An eight thousand token mission log needs sixty four million pairwise scores in every attention layer.

23
00:01:23.333 --> 00:01:27.167
Double it to sixteen thousand, and the bill is four times, not two.

24
00:01:28.367 --> 00:01:29.767
This shapes real design.

25
00:01:30.067 --> 00:01:32.433
Embedding a long log whole is expensive.

26
00:01:32.733 --> 00:01:35.300
That's why a RAG system chunks its documents.

27
00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:42.733
And why just increasing the context window is never free when your GPU latency budget is three hundred milliseconds.

28
00:01:43.933 --> 00:01:44.763
Let's recap.

29
00:01:44.763 --> 00:01:47.667
Each token blends all tokens, in parallel.

30
00:01:47.967 --> 00:01:49.867
Direct links replaced recurrence.

31
00:01:50.167 --> 00:01:52.167
It's just matrix multiplication.

32
00:01:52.467 --> 00:01:54.889
But cost grows as n squared.

33
00:01:54.889 --> 00:01:56.100
Next up: NLTK.
